{
	"Name": "Okta - Account & MFA Changes - High Number of Okta Password Reset or Unlock Events for One User",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Account & MFA Changes\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1110\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|High Number of Okta Password Reset or Unlock Events for One User\" or \"<ip>|High Number of Okta Password Reset or Unlock Events for One User\"\n\nThree or more password reset or account unlock events (self-service emails/SMS/voice, admin resets, unlock tokens) for one user within the search window. Repeated resets can be an attacker trying to take over the account through recovery flows.\n\nFalse positives: a user struggling with recovery.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_suspicious_okta_user_password_reset_or_unlock_attempts/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/defense_evasion_suspicious_okta_user_password_reset_or_unlock_attempts.toml",
	"GUID": "0d044dee-b02f-5434-b7da-3511c010c0e0",
	"Labels": [
		"okta",
		"detection",
		"account-mfa-changes",
		"credential-access",
		"T1110"
	],
	"Metadata": {
		"timeframe": null
	}
}